{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>I call heaven and earth to witness against you this day.</b> Some say the meaning of the witness of heaven and earth is the angels and human beings, and others said concerning the substance, like the meaning of \"your heaven [shall be] like iron and your earth like bronze.\" The correct view in my eyes is that they are witnesses in that they see them always, they and their children, for they stand, like the meaning of \"as the days of the heavens upon the earth,\" and likewise \"Hear, O mountains, the contention of YHWH,\" and likewise \"this stone shall be a witness unto us.\" And perhaps a disputant will argue that the heavens will melt away like smoke, and his companion — the disputant — is awake while his heart sleeps." "<b>תאבדון.</b> Like תלמדון, because it is not in construct state."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:17.107970750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}